WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.220
Hi guys, my name is Heinrich

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:05.250
and welcome to another coffee
break with Firm Learning.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.920
Today I'd like to talk
about the little things,

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.320
the little things that
may not seem important

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.310
at first sight, but can
really make a difference

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.760
how you are perceived in
your work environment.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.580
Personally, I like to call
these things hygiene factors.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.720
So if you wonder what a hygiene factor is,

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.050
let's think about a great hotel.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.070
It is super luxurious,
a great entrance hall

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.550
you have a personal Butler,
who brings to your food,

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.310
your luggage and everything
else you may need.

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:35.850
So at firsthand, it might
seem that this is just

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.800
an amazing experience
and a great day to be it

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.890
and actually imagine the following thing;

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.580
you're going to the bathroom
and you'll find the toilet

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:47.530
not being cleaned their hairs
of potentially previous guests

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:50.720
in your shower and adjust
does not seem clean

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.040
and nice as you would expect.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.890
What would be the impression
of this hotel now?

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:59.890
But for sure, nevermind all
the great Butler services

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.150
and luxurious wines and great
luxurious entrance halls

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.994
your experience, your
impression of that hotel

00:01:05.994 --> 00:01:07.970
will be over and this is due to something

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.600
that is called hygiene factors.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.950
These are factors that if
they are there by themselves,

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.810
they do not make a great impression

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:17.180
but if they're not there
anymore of their gun,

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.110
then this is super bad and your customer,

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:21.890
your professional, your work colleague,

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.970
we just have a very bad impression of you.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.180
Just as the hygiene and hotel,

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.800
the hotel may be as great as this might be

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.730
but if the toilet, the
bathroom is not hygienic,

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.660
then adjust the bad hotel.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.790
And there's similar things like that,

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.590
in the workplaces where
there are these little things

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:41.860
that if you do them, that
by itself will not be great.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:44.390
Nobody will say hey, this Tony guy,

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:47.050
he's so great because
he's doing these things.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:48.570
But if you don't do them,

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:51.930
then that actually might be
perceived as unprofessional

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:54.210
as not knowing the rules of the game

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.430
is just not being proud of the culture,

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:59.500
just not knowing how to behave in a good

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.430
and professional manner,
and you don't want that.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.800
So let's go over five things like that,

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:05.870
that are little things,

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:08.850
but I believe really make a difference.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.810
And these are some lessons
that I really learned

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.210
from my time at McKinsey,
where these things

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:15.120
are just perceived to be super basic,

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.650
you just need to follow these

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.380
kind of professional standards,

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:20.130
but this is not just to focus on dieting,

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:22.440
this is true for other
industry firms like that,

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.680
where these things are just important

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.570
and you do not want to stand out

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:28.690
by not doing these things right.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:31.760
So let's start with five
tips that really make

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.530
a difference in the
workplace and that you should

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:35.430
just get right in order to not

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.500
be perceived in a negative way.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.480
The first step is about
how you write your emails.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:42.750
And let me start with a little story here.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.860
A friend of mine recently started working

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:47.850
with a large venture capital
fund here in Germany.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:50.500
And he told me the story and
I just thought it was funny

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.560
so let me just share it because
when he was kind of applying

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:56.070
for the job and getting
those first interviews,

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.520
of course, the tone was super friendly,

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:01.650
he was writing this email
and getting these super nice

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.910
and friendly responses and so on.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:06.300
And then suddenly after he got hired,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.160
and kind of he wrote the very
first email in the same style,

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.970
he was always writing
them, and the first reply

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:14.890
he got from this direct supervisors,

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:18.360
and let's just call this
guy Tony, "Please, Tony,

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.470
from now on only and bullet points,

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:22.990
I only want to have
emails in bullet points."

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:26.310
And this might sound a
bit stupid and ridiculous

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.910
but I think this is really
to the point and important.

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:32.180
In work life, nobody wants
to read two paragraphs

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:35.540
of text of lots and lots of
words of super long email

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:38.230
of a page longer and so on, nobody wants

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.620
to read these kind of emails.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.620
If you write an email, make sure that

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.170
it's written in bullet points,

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.110
at least always if it goes kind of beyond

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:46.180
a couple of sentences.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:48.290
But if you have several
thoughts that you want to share,

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:51.280
never just write text, but
rather than bullet points,

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:54.470
each bullet point consists
of one argument, one thought,

00:03:54.470 --> 00:03:56.600
one point that you want to bring forward,

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.590
be concise, be to the point,

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.710
don't write fluff in your emails,

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:03.060
make it crisp and clear what you want.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.980
And this is just helpful to
everybody because otherwise,

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.490
you are just a waste of time.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:08.960
Nobody wants to do that, nobody wants

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.140
to read these kind of super long emails.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.187
My second tip also regards to emails

00:04:13.187 --> 00:04:15.120
but not what you write them down

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.540
but rather documents
attachments that you do.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.840
You see super frequently in businesses,

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.960
the people are sending raw attachments

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:23.940
with the name of something

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:28.070
like COPY OF COPY OF ATTACHMENT-597. XLSX

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:32.662
or something like that.

00:04:32.662 --> 00:04:35.320
So basically you have an
attachment with a name

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:38.400
that has just not been edited,
that just has been exported,

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.030
copied from whatever other program

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:44.090
and you don't have a keyword
I was in the attachment

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.410
just by reading the name.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:48.740
Guys this is just super unprofessional,

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:50.840
you cannot protect that
you cannot just send

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:54.410
these attachments with these
gibberish names like that.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:57.020
I mean, imagine all these
people needing to drag

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.530
and drop your attachment
maybe in their file structure

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:01.730
and they're file system
and all the need for first

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.890
look into it and then to give it a name,

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:06.440
how much more convenient
would it be to everybody,

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:09.830
if just you from the beginning
would have given a clear

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.200
and crisp name to that attachment,

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.730
that basically the
person would direct know

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:17.610
what is in the file, but
then could just drag the file

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:20.730
in his own file system
without needing to edit it

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:23.150
or to do any other
changes to the file name.

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:25.950
Be professional, name
your attachments in a way

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:29.040
that makes sense guys, otherwise,
it's just unprofessional.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:32.450
Don't do that, don't be
that guy, do it this way

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:33.900
and you'll be just fine.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.550
Third point is about your availability.

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:39.070
And here of course, the
culture might be different

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:40.270
from business to business.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:43.140
So this may be not related
to your specific business

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.450
to your specific organization,
but from my experiences

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:49.010
is something that is
just very well received

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:50.630
and widely appreciated.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:53.450
And situations are you available,

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:56.520
if your colleague, your
team leader or supervisor

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:00.360
or another person you work
with wants to reach out to you

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.970
and especially via phone.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:05.760
And personally, in my organization
where I currently work,

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:09.900
I know two or three people,
if I try to call them,

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:13.370
I just know that they will
not pick up at that moment.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:16.200
They are just not available on the phone,

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.500
I will not be able to know
just call them and reach them

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.140
and this is just annoying.

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:23.510
Maybe I just want to talk
about something with them

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:25.520
I would like to discuss a thought I have,

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:27.690
there's something maybe
super urgent and important

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:30.170
I'd like to address but these people

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:33.210
are just not approachable
and that's the problem.

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:35.920
And an organization's would
usually tend to happen

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:38.100
is that these people actually are called

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.720
less frequently than others,
they are considered less

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:41.820
than other colleagues.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:43.870
If I want to know something
want to discuss something

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:46.540
I rather call the guy
who I know will pick up

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:47.373
and will let me know what's going on

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:49.630
and if you have some time
for me, or maybe later.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:51.890
But if you are the guy who
never picks up his phone,

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:55.133
maybe even doesn't want to
because he feels bothered,

00:06:55.133 --> 00:06:58.343
feels like this is not the best
use of my time or whatever,

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.250
I will just not reach
out these people anymore.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:05.180
And in the short term,
this might be nice helpful,

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:07.690
you might feel like you have
more time to do other things,

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.760
but in the long term, this will
really hurt your reputation

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:12.450
and your standing organization.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.130
So do not do that.

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:16.600
And what I would advise, always make sure

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:18.890
if somehow possible to pick up

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:20.550
and if you do not have time at the moment,

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:23.540
just let the guy know, sorry,
right now is not a good time,

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:25.770
let me call you later,
let's call this evening,

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.340
let's have a call tomorrow.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:30.940
If you really cannot pick
up the phone right now

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:34.077
than at least directly
write a short text and say,

00:07:34.077 --> 00:07:36.720
"Sorry, can talk about now
we're recording later."

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:39.930
But be responsive, answer
let the other person know

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:42.670
what is going on and how she can reach you

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:44.800
because usually if somebody calls you

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:45.770
there's something important

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.590
that the person wants to discuss.

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:51.210
So don't just flake, don't
just tuck away from the corner

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:54.070
but take it and make sure you're reachable

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:56.280
for the important people
in your organization.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.800
The fourth tip is about
how you handle meetings

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:00.050
and meeting invites.

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:02.890
And sure, this might also
depend on the organization

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:06.430
and maybe at your place,
it's very different than some

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:10.130
but usually what what I observed
what is widely appreciated

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:11.960
almost all organizations is

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:14.880
making good use of calendar invites of

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:18.210
your outlook invite, calendar system

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:21.520
or the ICAL system, or
whatever you might use,

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.970
but make use of that.

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:25.730
So if you have a meeting,
make it a good habit of yours

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.840
of always sending out a calendar invite

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.570
to make sure that that person

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.710
directly has it in their calendar.

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:34.910
Because usually what will
happen and this person needs

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:38.520
to make the invite the
entry into calendar himself,

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:40.530
which of course takes
time and is annoying,

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:43.130
and especially if you're
hosting larger meetings

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:45.540
with more than only one counterpart

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:48.700
and every person needs
to do that by himself,

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:51.000
instead of you just doing
it once and then everybody

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.620
has a direct in the calendar.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:54.940
And of course, there are other
benefits to that as well,

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:58.230
if you reschedule it,
everybody directly sees it.

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:01.240
What you should of course,
also do is always enter

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:04.720
a location, if it's kind of out of office,

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:07.840
enter the exact address
where the other person

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:10.890
is supposed to go to just
enter the name of the hotel

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:12.540
or the name of the conference room

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:15.870
that you would like to go to
because it's just very annoying

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:19.170
and completely unprofessional
if the person just find that

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:21.853
and then it's to look it
up on Google or somewhere,

00:09:23.064 --> 00:09:25.400
just to know where you
actually intend to meet.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:27.080
And especially now imagine a situation

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.740
where you sit in a car, maybe
have your phone connected

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:33.580
to the navigation system,
you expect that the invite

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:37.440
has this info click on your
calendar, you open the invite,

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:39.890
and then just to find
that you cannot just click

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.060
on the address and it
will directly guide you

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.420
in the navigation to go there
which you would have expected

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:46.002
and you wouldn't have fall for

00:09:46.002 --> 00:09:47.130
but now that you just
find the name of the hotel

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:51.130
that now you need to independently
google and look out for.

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:53.100
I mean, again, guys, this is annoying,

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:54.140
this is unprofessional.

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:56.120
Don't be that guy, don't do that.

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:58.100
Always send out invites to make it easier

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.650
for everybody who's
supposed to participate

00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:02.090
and then also make sure that all

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:05.780
the relevant meeting
information is actually included

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:09.240
in this invite to make the
life easier for everybody

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:10.530
who's involved.

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:13.530
Now to my tip number five,
and this is about how

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:15.940
you actually handle meetings.

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:16.899
And one thing that I
believe is really crucial,

00:10:16.899 --> 00:10:21.899
but that many people don't do
is setting up proper agendas.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:24.790
If you set up a meeting,
if you invite somebody,

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.150
maybe even just the colleague,

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:29.260
you would like to talk
to about a few topics,

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:31.160
always make sure that in the invite,

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:33.570
or in the email that you
write them in advance,

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:35.770
they are kind of in a bullet style format,

00:10:35.770 --> 00:10:37.260
the things that you would like to talk,

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:39.550
the things that you would like to address.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:42.180
You know, meetings are just super annoying

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:44.670
if there's no invite, nobody really knows

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:46.460
what it's supposed to be all about,

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:49.260
nobody has an understanding
what the outcomes

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:51.290
are supposed to be of the meeting

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:52.540
and then you're sitting in the meeting

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.150
with the meeting organizer,

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:56.520
and often even the organizer himself

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:58.550
hasn't clearly thought that out

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.180
and then very often this meeting

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:02.550
are just completely unproductive.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:05.090
So again, please do your
very best to prepare,

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:07.520
let the other person know
what the meeting is supposed

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:10.610
to be all about to also give
the other person a chance

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:13.430
to prepare for himself,
'cause then the likelihood

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:16.550
of the meeting being a
success and yielding results

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:18.010
that are valuable for everybody

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:21.070
and being a good investment
of time for everybody involved

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:22.730
are just much higher.

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:25.480
Do that and everybody will
be happy and you will just

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:27.650
create a much more professional experience

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:28.733
in your organization.

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:32.330
So let me just to recap, five tips today,

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:35.160
little tips, little things,
where I believe though

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:37.450
that these things really
make a difference.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:39.720
First is about how you write emails.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.360
Make sure that then the bullet form type,

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:44.340
write bullet points,
don't write long text,

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:46.150
nobody wants to read long email.

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:48.390
Second point, make sure that you name

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:51.440
your attachments properly,
that people can just pick up

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.260
the attachment know what's
in, can directly stored

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:56.880
in the whole file system,
without any trouble anything

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.440
that's just kind of
annoying and nobody knows

00:11:58.440 --> 00:11:59.580
what's in there.

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:01.890
Third to this your availability.

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:03.650
Make sure that people can reach you.

00:12:03.650 --> 00:12:05.950
If you're calling pick up or
at least write a short text

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:09.440
letting the person know that
right now is not a good time

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:11.240
but you are of course
happy to reach out later.

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:15.180
Be available to the important
people in your organization.

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:17.830
Fourth is about how you
handle meeting invites.

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:20.060
Make sure that you always
send such an invite,

00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:22.330
and make sure that all
the relevant information

00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:25.450
is included in it, especially
the location of course,

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:27.440
also for instance, dial in information

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:30.530
for telephone conference,
anything like that.

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:32.970
And last but not least, meeting agendas.

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:34.800
If you talk to somebody set up a meeting

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:37.020
with an individual or
a group, make sure that

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:39.090
you let know the people in advance

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:41.030
what is expected of
them, what the agenda is,

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:43.480
what you hope to get out of the meeting.

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:46.380
Five things you may believe
these are the little things

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:48.490
and you're right they are
and probably if you do that,

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:51.020
it's not like everybody
would walk around and say

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:53.530
this Tony guy is the greatest guys of all.

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:55.890
But if you don't do these things,

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:57.300
with a high likelihood this

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:59.490
will fall back negatively on you.

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:02.400
It's like a hygiene factor,
it's like the toilet

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:04.700
that is not cleaned up
properly, get that right

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:05.980
and make a good thing out of that.

